description:
2026 California gubernatorial election will take place on November 3, 2026 following a top two jungle primary in June.&#x20;

Incumbent Gavin Newsom is term-limited and cannot run. As of February 2026, polling is heavily split, with major candidates polling below 20%, while it is unclear which party the top two candidates will receive.

Historically leans heavily Democratic, however with a split field it is possible for two Republicans to advance to the general.
